# Core Rules

- Treat `AGENTS.md` and the `docs/` folder as the project's persistent knowledge base.
- Before adding anything, search the repository for an existing equivalent.
- Reuse existing classes/components/services/queries/DTOs before creating new ones.
- Never solve the same business concept twice under different names.
- Do not invent requirements or silently make business decisions.
- Keep changes scoped to the requested task.
- For multi-file changes, plan first, then implement.
- Never modify migrations already applied to shared environments; create a new migration.
- Do not introduce a new library/package without explaining why it is needed.
- Run the smallest relevant build/test/validation after changes.
- If documentation and code disagree, identify the conflict instead of silently choosing one.
- Update the relevant documentation when architecture, domain behavior, API contracts, database structure, or project status changes.
